  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Emmara Tandris\u2019s ability prevents all damage that would be dealt to creature tokens you control, not just combat damage.",
      "oracle_id": "38a71429-e673-4de4-80a8-f59e5cf98acc",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Emmara Tandris is dealt lethal damage at the same creature tokens you control would be dealt damage, the damage that would be dealt to those tokens is prevented.",
      "oracle_id": "38a71429-e673-4de4-80a8-f59e5cf98acc",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a spell or ability is cast or activated that would have Goblin Furrier deal damage to a snow creature, and Goblin Furrier leaves the battlefield before it resolves, the damage won\u2019t be prevented.",
      "oracle_id": "3f086b72-6e7c-40d4-b995-d5f94c494462",
      "published_at": "2006-07-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a spell or ability damages multiple things, divide up the damage before applying this effect. This means you can\u2019t normally end up with an odd amount of damage on something.",
      "oracle_id": "68715465-6cf9-4006-87e9-31f227fe9ed3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you have two of these on the battlefield, the damage is multiplied by 4.",
      "oracle_id": "68715465-6cf9-4006-87e9-31f227fe9ed3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The multiplied damage counts in all ways as if it came from the original source. Furnace of Rath is not the source.",
      "oracle_id": "68715465-6cf9-4006-87e9-31f227fe9ed3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The trample rules cause damage to be divided before it is doubled.",
      "oracle_id": "68715465-6cf9-4006-87e9-31f227fe9ed3",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If multiple effects modify how damage will be dealt, the player who would be dealt damage or the controller of the creature that would be dealt damage chooses the order to apply the effects. For example, Mending Hands says, \u201cPrevent the next 4 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.\u201d Suppose a spell would deal 5 damage to a player who has cast Mending Hands targeting themselves. That player can either (a) prevent 4 damage first and then let Furnace of Rath double the remaining 1 damage, taking 2 damage, or (b) double the damage to 10 and then prevent 4 damage, taking 6 damage.",
      "oracle_id": "68715465-6cf9-4006-87e9-31f227fe9ed3",
      "published_at": "2005-08-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Rescue Retriever leaves the battlefield before combat damage is dealt to your other attacking Soldiers, they will take damage as normal. Notably, this means it is usually a bad idea to attack with Rescue Retriever if your opponent could block it with a creature that has first strike and enough power to kill it.",
      "oracle_id": "86f9897f-84aa-4c8d-8335-cfdb2f565311",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Rescue Retriever prevents damage to other attacking Soldiers even if it isn't also attacking.",
      "oracle_id": "86f9897f-84aa-4c8d-8335-cfdb2f565311",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Hindervines checks whether a creature has a +1/+1 counter on it at the moment it deals damage. It doesn't matter whether a creature had a +1/+1 counter, or was even on the battlefield, when Hindervines resolved.",
      "oracle_id": "8d13fabc-1e0f-41f2-8873-9f44b68f7e43",
      "published_at": "2013-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "\"Flashback [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.\"",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it's legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a flashback cost) you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can cast a spell using flashback even if it was somehow put into your graveyard without having been cast.",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must still follow any timing restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card's type. For instance, you can cast a sorcery using flashback only when you could normally cast a sorcery.",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any \u201centers\u201d triggered ability of the copied creature will trigger when the token enters the battlefield. Any \u201cas [this creature] enters\u201d or \u201c[this creature] enters with\u201d abilities of the chosen creature will also work.",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the copied creature has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the copied creature is a token, the token that\u2019s created copies the original characteristics of that token as stated by the effect that created the token.",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the copied creature is copying something else, then the token enters the battlefield as whatever that creature copied.",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The token copies exactly what was printed on the original creature and nothing else (unless that creature is copying something else or is a token; see below). It doesn\u2019t copy whether that creature is tapped or untapped, whether it has any counters on it or Auras and Equipment attached to it, or any non-copy effects that have changed its power, toughness, types, color, or so on.",
      "oracle_id": "9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.",
      "oracle_id": "a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Spells and abilities that replace or redirect damage are not affected by this card.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The \"damage can't be prevented\" statement overrides all forms of preventing damage. Damage prevention spells and abilities can still be cast and activated, they just don't do anything.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "\"Flashback [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.\"",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it's legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
